Subject: [PATCH] transmission: avoid Foundation UTF-8 helper on iPhoneOS

The CLI/daemon package does not need the macOS Foundation-backed UTF-8
autodetection helper. On iPhoneOS, including Foundation currently pulls in a
Procursus XPC header path that does not compile with the bundled SDK headers.
Use Transmission's generic invalid-UTF-8 replacement path instead.

diff -ruN -U0 a/libtransmission/CMakeLists.txt b/libtransmission/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/libtransmission/CMakeLists.txt	2026-07-06 00:00:00
+++ b/libtransmission/CMakeLists.txt	2026-07-06 00:00:00
@@ -20,0 +21,4 @@
+
+if(APPLE AND CMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT MATCHES "iPhoneOS")
+    set(IS_APPLE_CLANG FALSE)
+endif()
diff -ruN -U0 a/libtransmission/utils.cc b/libtransmission/utils.cc
--- a/libtransmission/utils.cc	2026-07-06 00:00:00
+++ b/libtransmission/utils.cc	2026-07-06 00:00:00
@@ -316 +316 @@
-#if !(defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__clang__))
+#if !(defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__clang__)) || defined(__ENVIRONMENT_IPHONE_OS_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__)
